====================================================================
               PART 10 - ISSABEL PUBLIC IP CONFIGURATION
====================================================================

RUN INSIDE ISSABEL 4.


First make a backup:

cp /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0 \
/root/ifcfg-eth0.backup


Check the backup exists:

ls -l /root/ifcfg-eth0.backup


Edit:

vi /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0


In vi:

Press:

Esc

Then:

:%d

Press Enter.


Press:

i


Enter:

DEVICE=eth0
TYPE=Ethernet
ONBOOT=yes
BOOTPROTO=none
IPADDR=61.245.30.75
NETMASK=255.255.255.248
GATEWAY=61.245.30.73
DNS1=8.8.8.8
DNS2=1.1.1.1


Save:

Press Esc

Type:

:wq

Press Enter.


====================================================================
                    PART 11 - RESTART NETWORK
====================================================================

RUN INSIDE ISSABEL.


systemctl restart network


Wait several seconds.

Check:

ip -br addr


Expected:

eth0    UP    61.245.30.75/29


Check route:

ip route


Expected:

default via 61.245.30.73 dev eth0


There should NOT be:

192.168.10.187


as Issabel's main IP anymore.


====================================================================
                    PART 12 - TEST NETWORK
====================================================================

RUN INSIDE ISSABEL.


TEST 1 - Interface:

ip -br addr


Expected:

eth0 UP 61.245.30.75/29


TEST 2 - Gateway:

ping -c 4 61.245.30.73


Expected:

4 packets transmitted
4 received


TEST 3 - Internet by IP:

ping -c 4 8.8.8.8


Expected successful replies.


TEST 4 - DNS:

ping -c 4 google.com


Expected successful replies.


If:

gateway ping works
Internet IP ping works
DNS ping works


then the public network is functioning correctly.


====================================================================
                  PART 13 - WEB MANAGEMENT
====================================================================

From a PC that can reach the public IP:

https://61.245.30.75


If necessary:

http://61.245.30.75


If HTTPS shows a certificate warning, the Issabel server may be
using a self-signed certificate.


If the web page does not open, RUN INSIDE ISSABEL:

systemctl status httpd


Then:

netstat -tulpn | grep -E ':80|:443'


Then:

curl -I http://127.0.0.1


These commands determine whether Apache is running and listening.


