====================================================================
                         TROUBLESHOOTING
====================================================================

PROBLEM:
enp2s0 shows DOWN


RUN:

ip link set enp2s0 up

ethtool enp2s0 | grep "Link detected"


If "no":

Check cable/switch/NIC.


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
enp2s0 is UP but vmbr1 is DOWN


RUN:

cat /etc/network/interfaces

Check:

auto vmbr1
iface vmbr1 inet manual
        bridge-ports enp2s0
        bridge-stp off
        bridge-fd 0


Then:

ifreload -a

Then:

ip -br link

Then:

bridge link


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
Issabel eth0 says Link detected: no


RUN ON PROXMOX:

ethtool enp2s0 | grep "Link detected"

Must say:

yes


Then:

bridge link | grep enp2s0


Must show:

master vmbr1


Then:

qm config 200


Must show:

bridge=vmbr1


Then restart VM if necessary.


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
Issabel has link but no Internet


INSIDE ISSABEL:

ip -br addr

ip route


Verify:

61.245.30.75/29

default via 61.245.30.73


Test:

ping -c 4 61.245.30.73

ping -c 4 8.8.8.8

ping -c 4 google.com


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
Internet works but web management doesn't open


INSIDE ISSABEL:

systemctl status httpd

netstat -tulpn | grep -E ':80|:443'

curl -I http://127.0.0.1


If Apache is not running:

systemctl start httpd


Then:

systemctl enable httpd


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
SIP registration works but no audio


Check:

1. Public IP
2. Asterisk external IP
3. RTP range
4. Firewall
5. SIP provider IPs
6. SIP transport
7. NAT settings


Do NOT randomly open ports.


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
Inbound call works but outbound doesn't


Check:

1. SIP trunk
2. Outbound route
3. Dial pattern
4. Provider authentication
5. Caller ID requirements
6. SIP provider restrictions
7. Firewall


--------------------------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM:
Outbound call works but inbound doesn't


Check:

1. SIP trunk registration
2. Provider inbound routing
3. DID configuration
4. Inbound route
5. SIP signaling
6. Firewall


